    "memory_register_menu": "Camera Set. Memory",
    "memory_dial_hint": "turning the dial to {m}",
    "memories_title": "Memories {list}",
    "memories_intro": "The camera's mode-dial memories. Each holds a copy of the shooting settings registered into it.",
    "save_load_path": "MENU > Setup > Reset/Save Settings > Save/Load Settings > Save",
    "max_settings_files_on_card": 10,
    "connect_network_steps": [
      "Unplug any USB cable between the camera and a computer: while one is in, the camera does not answer on the network.",
      "Wired: MENU > Network > Wired LAN > Wired LAN Connect: On. Wi-Fi: MENU > Network > Wi-Fi > Wi-Fi Connect: On, joined to the same network as this computer.",
      "MENU > Network > Cnct./Remote Sht. > Remote Shoot Function: On.",
      "MENU > Network > Network Option > Access Authen. Settings: On, with a user name and password. Enter the same pair once in the desktop app's Connect to the camera; it is kept in a private file on that computer, never in the settings file.",
      "Leave the camera on the shooting screen: it refuses while in playback, in a menu dialog, or with the mode dial on 1, 2 or 3."
    ],
    "connect_network_note": "Careful: loading a settings file in which Wired LAN Connect or Wi-Fi Connect is Off drops the camera off the network. The editor warns before sending such a file.",
    "connect_usb_steps": [
      "MENU > Setup > USB > USB Connection Mode: PC Remote (with Sel. When Connect, choose PC Remote on the camera's screen when the cable goes in). Mass Storage and MTP do not work.",
      "A memory card must be in the camera.",
      "Connect the cable; the camera shows the remote-shooting screen. Quit Image Capture, Photos, Lightroom or anything else that may hold the camera.",
      "Leave the camera on the shooting screen: it refuses while in playback or with the mode dial on 1, 2 or 3."
    ],
    "address_hint": "MENU > Network > Wired LAN > Display Wired LAN Info., or Wi-Fi > Display Wi-Fi Info.",
    "read_failed_usb": "Check the camera is on, joined by a cable that carries data, with USB Connection Mode on PC Remote (MENU > Setup > USB), and on the shooting screen, not with the mode dial on 1, 2 or 3. The steps are in Connect to the camera.",
    "read_failed_network": "Check the camera is on and on the same network as this computer, with Wired LAN Connect or Wi-Fi Connect on, Remote Shoot Function on and Access Authen. Settings set, on the shooting screen (not with the mode dial on 1, 2 or 3), and with no USB cable to a computer: while one is in, the camera does not answer on the network. The steps are in Connect to the camera.",
    "volatile_note": "Only the {n} load toggle flag(s) differ, which flip on every load: the camera holds what was written.",
